{
	"maps": {
		"main": {
			"note": "黑松山 from the 玉螺湖村 road: the 黄土大道 runs west off the village's highway and turns north past a roadside tea house to the crossing, then north-east between the paddies of the 山脚乡田 to the foot of the mountain. The narrow path winds up the west side among the boulders to the granite street west of the chasm; the 铁索桥 crosses it to the east street, which goes straight down to the foot. Both streets climb to the gate of 黑松堡 (黑松淳于 on its golden board); behind the gate a walled 夹道 ends at a boulder, arrows waiting in its walls. Beside the gate the clifftops run east and west under the vine-covered castle walls: climbed, they let one into the west and east gardens. Inside, 黑松阁's west hall opens on the west and north gardens, the main hall and the shut storeroom; the east hall on the east garden (its dogs) and the south garden. Each hall has its stairs up to 淳于's rooms.",
